IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sda-common`
IMPORT `taa-procedure`

-- Taxation Administration Act 2007 (NT) -- cases for the procedure core (taa-procedure.l4).
--
-- Expected values worked by hand from the deposited reprint REPT039 (ss 21, 27, 34-36, 41-43, 107-117, 128), never
-- copied from the encoding's output. Clock for the regulative rules: days.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Not an official version of the Taxation Administration Act 2007; see SOURCE-LICENSE.md.

§ `Cases -- the taxpayer, and the applicant for a first home owner grant`

§§ `s 27 -- rounding down to 5 cents`

#ASSERT `rounded down to a multiple of 5 cents` 10414.2969 EQUALS 10414.25
#ASSERT `rounded down to a multiple of 5 cents` 25987.53425625 EQUALS 25987.5
#ASSERT `rounded down to a multiple of 5 cents` 100 EQUALS 100
#ASSERT `rounded down to a multiple of 5 cents` 0.04 EQUALS 0

§§ `s 21(4) -- the 5-year limit on reassessment`

GIVEN `reassessed on` IS A DATE
      `to give effect to an objection` IS A BOOLEAN
      `non-disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN
      `authorised by the taxation law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `applied within 5 years` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Reassessment facts`
`a reassessment of a 1 March 2020 assessment` MEANS
    `Reassessment facts` WITH
        `the date of the initial assessment`                                         IS YMD 2020 3 1
        `the date of the reassessment`                                               IS `reassessed on`
        `it gives effect to a decision on an objection, review or appeal`            IS `to give effect to an objection`
        `the taxpayer failed to make a full and true disclosure and was assessed too low` IS `non-disclosure`
        `the taxation law authorises a reassessment after 5 years`                   IS `authorised by the taxation law`
        `the taxpayer applied in writing for the reassessment within 5 years`       IS `applied within 5 years`

-- Five years to the day is not "more than 5 years"; the next day is.
#ASSERT `the Commissioner can make the reassessment` (`a reassessment of a 1 March 2020 assessment` (YMD 2025 3 1) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the Commissioner can make the reassessment` (`a reassessment of a 1 March 2020 assessment` (YMD 2025 3 2) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
-- (c): the Stamp Duty Act's "even though the time limit ... has passed" (for example s 90D(8)); (d): applied in time.
#ASSERT `the Commissioner can make the reassessment` (`a reassessment of a 1 March 2020 assessment` (YMD 2028 3 2) FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the Commissioner can make the reassessment` (`a reassessment of a 1 March 2020 assessment` (YMD 2026 3 2) FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `the Commissioner can make the reassessment` (`a reassessment of a 1 March 2020 assessment` (YMD 2026 3 2) FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)

§§ `ss 107, 109-111 -- objecting`

#ASSERT `it is a relevant decision` `a first home owner grant decision`
#ASSERT NOT (`it is a relevant decision` `a decision not to make a reassessment`)
-- s 109(2): a reassessment from $20 000 to $25 000 is open to objection only as to the $5 000 increase.
#ASSERT `the amount open to objection` `an assessment or reassessment of duty` TRUE 20000 25000 EQUALS 5000
#ASSERT `the amount open to objection` `an assessment or reassessment of duty` TRUE 25000 20000 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the amount open to objection` `an assessment or reassessment of duty` FALSE 0 25000 EQUALS 25000
#ASSERT `the amount open to objection` `a decision not to make a reassessment` FALSE 0 25000 EQUALS 0
-- s 110(1): 60 days; s 111: longer only on a written application and a reasonable excuse.
#ASSERT `the days to object` EQUALS 60
#ASSERT `the days allowed to object` FALSE 0 EQUALS 60
#ASSERT `the days allowed to object` TRUE 90 EQUALS 90
#ASSERT `the time to object may be extended` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the time to object may be extended` FALSE TRUE)

§§ `ss 114-117 -- review or appeal`

#ASSERT `where the objection can go next` `a first home owner grant decision` `the objection is disallowed` EQUALS `to NTCAT for review only`
#ASSERT `where the objection can go next` `an assessment or reassessment of duty` `the objection is allowed in part only` EQUALS `to NTCAT for review, or to the Supreme Court on appeal, but not both`
#ASSERT `where the objection can go next` `an assessment or reassessment of duty` `the objection is allowed in full` EQUALS `nowhere: the objection was allowed in full`
#ASSERT `the days to apply for review or to appeal` EQUALS 60
-- Object on day 30; disallowed on day 90; Supreme Court appeal on day 140 (50 days later): all in time.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`Part 11 -- object within the time allowed, then review or appeal within 60 days` `an assessment or reassessment of duty` 60) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the person affected by the decision` `lodge a written objection stating the grounds fully and in detail` 30), (EVENT `the decision maker` (`give written notice of the decision on the objection` `the objection is disallowed`) 90), (EVENT `the person affected by the decision` `appeal to the Supreme Court against the decision on the objection` 140)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- A grant decision: NTCAT on day 100.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`Part 11 -- object within the time allowed, then review or appeal within 60 days` `a first home owner grant decision` 60) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the person affected by the decision` `lodge a written objection stating the grounds fully and in detail` 30), (EVENT `the decision maker` (`give written notice of the decision on the objection` `the objection is disallowed`) 90), (EVENT `the person affected by the decision` `apply to NTCAT for review of the decision on the objection` 100)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- Allowed in full: nothing more.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`Part 11 -- object within the time allowed, then review or appeal within 60 days` `an assessment or reassessment of duty` 60) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the person affected by the decision` `lodge a written objection stating the grounds fully and in detail` 30), (EVENT `the decision maker` (`give written notice of the decision on the objection` `the objection is allowed in full`) 90)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- An objection on day 70 is out of time: the decision maker owes no decision on it.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`Part 11 -- object within the time allowed, then review or appeal within 60 days` `an assessment or reassessment of duty` 60) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the person affected by the decision` `lodge a written objection stating the grounds fully and in detail` 70)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: the decision maker's written notice of the decision, pending (objection in time on day 30)
#TRACE `Part 11 -- object within the time allowed, then review or appeal within 60 days` `an assessment or reassessment of duty` 60 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the person affected by the decision` DOES `lodge a written objection stating the grounds fully and in detail` AT 30
-- expect: the NTCAT application still open -- a grant decision cannot go to the Supreme Court (s 115(2))
#TRACE `Part 11 -- object within the time allowed, then review or appeal within 60 days` `a first home owner grant decision` 60 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the person affected by the decision` DOES `lodge a written objection stating the grounds fully and in detail` AT 30
    PARTY `the decision maker` DOES `give written notice of the decision on the objection` `the objection is disallowed` AT 90
    PARTY `the person affected by the decision` DOES `appeal to the Supreme Court against the decision on the objection` AT 100

§§ `s 128 -- objecting does not stop payment`

#ASSERT NOT (`an objection suspends recovery of the tax`)
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 128 -- the duty must still be paid while the objection runs` 60 `an assessment or reassessment of duty` 60) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the taxpayer` `pay the duty` 50), (EVENT `the person affected by the decision` `lodge a written objection stating the grounds fully and in detail` 55), (EVENT `the decision maker` (`give written notice of the decision on the objection` `the objection is allowed in full`) 80)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the taxpayer, "s 128: an objection does not suspend the recovery of the tax ..." (objected, never paid)
#TRACE `s 128 -- the duty must still be paid while the objection runs` 60 `an assessment or reassessment of duty` 60 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the person affected by the decision` DOES `lodge a written objection stating the grounds fully and in detail` AT 10
    (WAITUNTIL 61)

§§ `ss 39, 41-43 -- penalty tax`

GIVEN `default`       IS A NUMBER
      `beyond control` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reasonable care` IS A BOOLEAN
      `intentional`   IS A BOOLEAN
      `concealment`   IS A BOOLEAN
      `hindered`      IS A BOOLEAN
      `cooperated`    IS A BOOLEAN
      `disclosed`     IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Penalty tax facts`
`a default` MEANS
    `Penalty tax facts` WITH
        `the amount of the tax default`                                                          IS `default`
        `the default arose from circumstances beyond the taxpayer's control and was rectified`  IS `beyond control`
        `the taxpayer took reasonable care to comply`                                            IS `reasonable care`
        `the default arose from intentional disregard of a taxation law`                         IS `intentional`
        `information was deliberately concealed or suppressed from the Commissioner`             IS `concealment`
        `the assessment or investigation was hindered in any other way`                          IS `hindered`
        `the Commissioner investigated and the taxpayer cooperated fully`                        IS `cooperated`
        `before any investigation, full and immediate disclosure avoided the need for one`       IS `disclosed`

-- A $10 000 default: 25% = $2 500; reasonable care 10% = $1 000; intentional disregard 75% = $7 500; with
-- concealment too 95% = $9 500; beyond the taxpayer's control and rectified: nil.
#ASSERT `the penalty tax` (`a default` 10000 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS 2500
#ASSERT `the penalty tax` (`a default` 10000 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS 1000
#ASSERT `the penalty tax` (`a default` 10000 FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS 7500
#ASSERT `the penalty tax` (`a default` 10000 FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS 9500
#ASSERT `the penalty tax` (`a default` 10000 TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS 0
-- s 42: $70 at 25% is $17.50, under $20: none. $80 at 25% is $20: imposed.
#ASSERT `the penalty tax` (`a default` 70 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the penalty tax` (`a default` 80 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS 20
-- s 41(3): full disclosure before any investigation: up to 80% off $2 500, leaving $500; full cooperation in an
-- investigation: up to 20%, leaving $2 000; concealment: no reduction, $7 500 stays.
#ASSERT `the least penalty tax after a s 41(3) reduction` (`a default` 10000 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS 500
#ASSERT `the least penalty tax after a s 41(3) reduction` (`a default` 10000 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS 2000
#ASSERT `the least penalty tax after a s 41(3) reduction` (`a default` 10000 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS 7500
-- Finding 23. Hindering the assessment in another way, with no concealment, is a s 41(2)(c)(ii) ground (75% = $7 500;
-- with intentional disregard 95% = $9 500), but the s 41(3) bar names only concealment or suppression, so the reduction
-- stays open: up to 80% off $7 500 leaves $1 500; up to 20% off leaves $6 000.
#ASSERT `the penalty tax` (`a default` 10000 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS 7500
#ASSERT `the penalty tax` (`a default` 10000 FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS 9500
#ASSERT `the least penalty tax after a s 41(3) reduction` (`a default` 10000 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS 1500
#ASSERT `the least penalty tax after a s 41(3) reduction` (`a default` 10000 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS 6000
#ASSERT `the most the Commissioner may reduce penalty tax by under s 41(3), percent` (`a default` 10000 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS 80
-- Concealment and hindering together: still no reduction.
#ASSERT `the most the Commissioner may reduce penalty tax by under s 41(3), percent` (`a default` 10000 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS 0
-- A $100 default: $25, less 80% = $5, under $20: none.
#ASSERT `the least penalty tax after a s 41(3) reduction` (`a default` 100 FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS 0
-- s 43: at least 14 days to pay, whatever the notice says.
#ASSERT `the days to pay penalty tax` 7 EQUALS 14
#ASSERT `the days to pay penalty tax` 30 EQUALS 30
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 43 -- pay the penalty tax within the period in the notice, at least 14 days` 7) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the taxpayer` `pay the penalty tax` 14)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the taxpayer, "s 43: ..." (paid on day 15)
#TRACE `s 43 -- pay the penalty tax within the period in the notice, at least 14 days` 7 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the taxpayer` DOES `pay the penalty tax` AT 15

§§ `ss 34-36 -- interest`

-- The market rates are inputs, one for each financial year (s 35(2)); the figures used here are made up for the tests.
-- $10 000 duty and $2 500 penalty tax unpaid from 1 July 2026 to 12 September 2026 (73 days, all in 2026-27), market
-- rate 4.35% + 8% premium = 12.35%: 12 500 x 12.35% x 73/365 = $308.75.
#ASSERT `the interest on the tax default` 10000 2500 (LIST 4.35) (YMD 2026 7 1) (YMD 2026 9 12) EQUALS `the interest, in dollars, is` 308.75
-- $1 000 for 5 days: $1.69, under $20: none (s 36).
#ASSERT `the interest on the tax default` 1000 0 (LIST 4.35) (YMD 2026 7 1) (YMD 2026 7 6) EQUALS `the interest, in dollars, is` 0
#ASSERT `the premium interest rate on` (YMD 2008 6 30) EQUALS 7
#ASSERT `the premium interest rate on` (YMD 2008 7 1) EQUALS 8
-- Finding 22. Across a 30 June: $10 000 unpaid from 1 June 2026 to 31 July 2026. 1-30 June (30 days) at 4.10% + 8% =
-- 12.10%: 10 000 x 12.10% x 30/365 = 36 300/365; 1-30 July (30 days) at 4.35% + 8% = 12.35%: 37 050/365. Together
-- 73 350/365 = $200.9589..., rounded down to $200.95. One rate of 4.35% for all 60 days would give 74 100/365 = $203.00.
#ASSERT `the interest on the tax default` 10000 0 (LIST 4.10, 4.35) (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2026 7 31) EQUALS `the interest, in dollars, is` 200.95
-- Across 30 June 2008, when the premium rose from 7% to 8%: $10 000 from 1 June 2008 to 31 July 2008 at market rates of
-- 7% then 7.5%: 30 days at 14% (42 000/365) and 30 days at 15.5% (46 500/365), 88 500/365 = $242.4657..., so $242.45.
#ASSERT `the interest on the tax default` 10000 0 (LIST 7, 7.5) (YMD 2008 6 1) (YMD 2008 7 31) EQUALS `the interest, in dollars, is` 242.45
-- Paid on 1 July: the 30 days of June are all in the first year, so one rate is enough: 36 300/365 = $99.4520..., $99.45.
#ASSERT `the interest on the tax default` 10000 0 (LIST 4.10) (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2026 7 1) EQUALS `the interest, in dollars, is` 99.45
-- Paid on 2 July with only one rate given: the period runs into a year with no rate, so not covered.
#ASSERT `the interest on the tax default` 10000 0 (LIST 4.10) (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2026 7 2) EQUALS `the interest is not covered` `the tax default runs into a financial year for which no market interest rate is given; the market interest rate is set for each financial year (TAA s 35(2)) and is not in the deposited texts`
#ASSERT `the 1 July after` (YMD 2026 6 30) EQUALS (YMD 2026 7 1)
#ASSERT `the 1 July after` (YMD 2026 7 1) EQUALS (YMD 2027 7 1)
